[{"source":"security","severity":"note","category":"boundary","title":"fold-check hex args lack length/overflow validation — over-length input silently wraps u64","location":"harness/fold_check.odin:32-38","evidence":"prev_hash_raw, okh := strconv.parse_uint(prev_hash_hex, 16) // uint in this Odin\n\tprev_tick1_raw, okt := strconv.parse_uint(prev_tick1_hex, 16)\n\tprev_hash_u := u64(prev_hash_raw)\n\tprev_tick1_u := u64(prev_tick1_raw)\n\tif !okh || !okt {\n\t\tfmt.eprintfln(\"fold-check: want <prev-catalog-hash-hex> <prev-tick1-hex> (16-digit hex)\")\n\t\treturn 2\n\t}","detail":"parse_uint(base 16) routes to strconv.parse_u64_of_base, whose loop `value *= u64(base); value += v` has no overflow guard; a >16-digit all-hex arg wraps and still returns ok=true, so the stated 16-digit contract is unenforced.","recommended_fix":"Validate len(prev_hash_hex)==16 and len(prev_tick1_hex)==16 (or range) before parsing, and reject with exit 2 otherwise; never splice a wrapped value."}]
